course: dictionary
lesson: 7783
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word python is a good example. «A python wrapped itself around the branch and squeezed.» The clues are wrapped, branch and squeezed, so a python here is a large snake.
explain: «Python is easy to read, so many schools use it to teach coding.» The clues are coding and easy to read. A capital P names a programming language, so that is the meaning that fits. Always ask: what does the sentence need? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Clues can be small words too. A python is not venomous, so it does not use poison. When you see a word that could mean two things, read the whole sentence before you choose.
fact: A python is a large snake that is not venomous.
fact: A python kills its prey by wrapping round it and squeezing.
fact: Pythons live in Africa, Asia and Australia.
fact: Python, with a capital P, is a popular programming language that is easy to read.
fact: Snakes are cold-blooded, so a big python can go months without a meal.
exercise: «A python wrapped itself around the branch and squeezed.» What is a python in this sentence? | A computer language | *A large snake that is not venomous | A tree with yellow bark | A river in southern Africa
exercise: «Python is easy to read, so many schools teach it to pupils learning to code.» Which meaning fits? | *A programming language | A tinned meat | A snake that squeezes its prey | A type of fever tree
exercise: «Pythons live in Africa, Asia and Australia.» Which place is NOT on this list? | Australia | Asia | *Europe | Africa
test: «A python does not use poison; it wraps round its prey and squeezes.» What does prey mean here? | A kind of programming language | *An animal that is hunted for food | A tree with yellow bark | A tool for squeezing
test: Priya says, «I wrote my first script in Python last night.» What does Python mean here? | *A programming language | A long river | A tinned meat | A large snake
exam: «Rosa's python script ran in seconds, so she showed her teacher.» What does python mean here? | *A programming language used to write a script | A tinned meat | A snake that squeezes its prey | A river in Africa
